From: d-b-c-e <anthony.mason1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:51:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(input): isolate raw wheels before sdl admission (FH2
 port)

Cherry-pick of 0301093d (nepo, FH1) onto 59bc11f5 alone, without its
parent 93a7e432 (resolved-action remap seam), for the FH2 Windows build.

Optional pre-attach device path policy: InputSystem::ConfigureDevicePaths
installs exact OS interface paths to exclude before AttachWindow; the SDL
driver then skips them before SDL_OpenGamepad and before the raw wheel's
SDL_OpenJoystick. No policy installed means no change.

Port adjustments: the "Resolved actions" test case and the remap_seam
fixture CMake (both from 93a7e432) are left out; FakeDriver loses `final`
so the device-path test can derive from it, as on 93a7e432.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HCiQ6QkyRFnhfXfshrj6tE
